{
 "product": "GitHub Copilot CLI (github/copilot-cli, v1.0.114, the real `copilot -p` headless loop)",
 "component": "The real Copilot CLI v1.0.114 `copilot -p` headless loop (the shipped non-interactive prompt mode, `--output-format json`) running the real Copilot CLI agent loop against the Trustrun tool set (search_docs, calculator, plus the monitor/grader/clarification tools run_audit adds) as real MCP tools executed in-process behind an HTTP bridge. The stub model is injected via the CLI's own BYOK path (COPILOT_PROVIDER_BASE_URL -> local OpenAI-compatible stub server; no GitHub sign-in). The stub's tool decisions are rendered as direct `trustrun-<name>` tool calls; the MCP server executes each call through the bridge and Copilot CLI feeds the bare tool text back as the next tool message. The driver runs under the project venv python and drives the published npm package's native binary as one subprocess per call. No key, no network. The loop ends on a text response, so multi-hop tasks can complete. Tool results reach the model verbatim as bare-text tool messages.",
 "version": "Copilot CLI 1.0.114 (tag v1.0.114; commit a9b36a75fd67e99da321b0088202dd7c19c3c492, 2026-11-17T16:35:44+00:00; license GitHub Copilot CLI License (proprietary); main HEAD 020bbc0a39e97deaf58327cb880167f845461690, 2026-11-18T05:59:27Z)",
 "repo": "https://github.com/github/copilot-cli",
 "repo_resolved": "https://github.com/github/copilot-cli, tag v1.0.114 (commit a9b36a75fd67e99da321b0088202dd7c19c3c492, 2026-11-17T16:35:44+00:00; release published 2026-11-18T05:59:26Z). Default-branch HEAD (020bbc0a39e97deaf58327cb880167f845461690, 2026-11-18T05:59:27Z) is 1 commit NEWER than the release, so the audited code is the 1.0.114 release, NOT HEAD. SECURITY.md ABSENT at the tag root; GitHub Security Advisories exist for the repo (https://github.com/github/copilot-cli/security/advisories/new). Assessment only -- nobody contacted, no draft written.. The audited object is the Copilot CLI `copilot -p` headless loop -- see the adapter docstring for the wiring facts.",
 "model_driver": "deterministic-stub-v1 (literal model: follows instructions in task text and tool output; the audit-30 DeterministicChatModel decision logic ported VERBATIM into n8n-stub.py, rendered as direct trustrun-<name> tool calls by real_agents/copilot_cli/copilot_cli_stub.py; see real_agents/copilot_cli_adapter.py and trustrun-venvs/copilot-cli-requests.jsonl)",
